### Implementation of Custom (User-Defined) Exceptions in Java

#### 1. Why Custom Exceptions are Required:
Standard exceptions (like `NullPointerException` or `ArithmeticException`) represent generic runtime faults. In enterprise and academic applications, errors must communicate domain-specific failures (e.g., `InsufficientBalanceException`, `RangeException`, `InvalidCredentialsException`).

#### 2. Design Principles for Custom Exceptions:
- **Inheritance Base:** 
  - Extend `Exception` to enforce compile-time verification (checked).
  - Extend `RuntimeException` for programmatic logic errors (unchecked).
- **Constructor Delegation:** Always invoke `super(message)` and `super(message, cause)` to retain root-cause chaining and printable stack traces.
- **Serialization:** Provide `serialVersionUID` for safe cross-network transfer.

#### 3. Complete University Problem Solution (Student Examination Mark Sheet):
> *Problem:* Read student marks in 6 subjects (0–50). If marks fall outside this range, throw a custom `RangeException`, else calculate percentage.

```java
// Step 1: Define Custom Exception
class RangeException extends Exception {
    private static final long serialVersionUID = 1L;

    public RangeException(String message) {
        super(message);
    }
}

// Step 2: Application Utilizing Custom Exception
public class StudentMarkSheetSystem {

    public static void validateMarks(int marks, String subject) throws RangeException {
        if (marks < 0 || marks > 50) {
            throw new RangeException("Mark " + marks + " for " + subject + " is invalid! Must be between 0 and 50.");
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String studentName = "Priya Sharma";
        int[] marks = { 45, 48, 52, 38, 42, 40 }; // 52 triggers RangeException
        String[] subjects = { "Maths", "Java", "COA", "OS", "DBMS", "SE" };

        int total = 0;
        boolean errorOccurred = false;

        System.out.println("Processing Grade Sheet for: " + studentName);

        for (int i = 0; i < marks.length; i++) {
            try {
                validateMarks(marks[i], subjects[i]);
                total += marks[i];
            } catch (RangeException re) {
                System.err.println("Academic Exception: " + re.getMessage());
                errorOccurred = true;
                break;
            }
        }

        if (!errorOccurred) {
            double percentage = (total / 300.0) * 100.0;
            System.out.printf("Total Marks: %d / 300\n", total);
            System.out.printf("Percentage: %.2f%%\n", percentage);
            System.out.println("Result: PASSED");
        } else {
            System.err.println("Result: FAILED - Mark evaluation halted due to RangeException.");
        }
    }
}
```

$$\therefore \text{Custom exceptions guarantee strict enforcement of university examination domain rules.}$$
